<BaseLayout title="Modifying a Motor's State Feedback — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Modifying a Motor's State Feedback</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A controller that measures the motor's own states can cancel the feedback
    paths the hardware already has. Back-EMF is one of those paths — and it was
    supplying most of the motor's low-frequency disturbance rejection.
    Decoupling it buys an electrical loop you can tune on its own and costs
    almost all of that stiffness. All three of the lecture's cases are the same
    expression with two terms switched on.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
